    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d991">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1048"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 256.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your unnumbered instruction of August 12, 1902.</p>
                <p>I shall lose no time in acquainting the Sublime Porte with the contents of the
                    circular instruction<anchor n="a" xml:id="d991-f1"/> therein inclosed which
                    deals with the situation of the Jews in Roumania.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John G. A.
                    Leishman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
